			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fosstodon.org/@eleventy\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>eleventy</span></a></span> Yeah this is something I've been thinking about a lot and is really frustrating. The fomo is real, especially for tech twitter, because they're still thriving over there... Occasionally they'll complain about the deterioration of the platform but are still clinging to the audiences and klout they've built. I don't blame them If my engagement on the platform was better I might not of switched...</p>",
