			},
			"date": "2023-03-08T23:26:20.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fosstodon.org/@eleventy\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>eleventy</span></a></span> I think it's fine to make compromised.</p><p>I try to not engage in hyper-consumerism but I still have an Apple laptop and a smartphone, but they're both over 6 years old. </p><p>It could be a good strategy to actually have a brand on Twitter for generic comms and then, through convos redirecting more developed content, tips, recipes, etc... on Mastodon.</p><p>Can be disappointed that the flood did not happen, but you can still push the waves :)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
